## 1. The system under test

Component: `runtime/company_runtime.py`
Recently changed: `StepRequest.prompt()` now carries dependency context via a `Handoff` dataclass (AGENT-09, completed today — observations 6737–6740). Before that change, a downstream step received the original request and nothing else, which is failure condition **F2** built directly into the code. That defect is fixed and has test coverage. This run is the first end-to-end exercise of the fix outside its own unit tests.

Also recently changed and relevant: cross-platform runtime fixes (ARCH-02, S970/S971) — `fcntl` import failures and path translation on Windows. This matters because assumption **A4** is precisely about those. They passed their tests. A test suite passing is not the same as a full run passing on this machine; if they resurface, per A4 that is the finding.

So: two recent fixes, both directly on the load-bearing path of this run. That is not a coincidence — it is why now is the right time to walk it.

